{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Each man his brother and each man his near one.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say <b>and each man his near one</b> after it already said \"his brother,\" which is the closest of the close? Indeed, it may intend to say that there are brothers whose feelings are distant one from the other, and with other people who are not relatives they will feel a soul-love — and this follows from the root of the souls, for there are souls that are close in their root yet come into being through distant parents, and there are souls that are distant in their root yet come into being through close parents, and they will love those close in the proximity of the root more than those close by virtue of parentage. To those close by virtue of parentage the name of brotherhood is ascribed, and to those close in their root the name of near one is ascribed. Accordingly, Scripture speaks of both aspects, and the one is above the other."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:10.200737792Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}